From 90b3e1d1020f6d16955c9ace93073704271a30a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: huangyifeng <huangyifeng@eswincomputing.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Feb 2025 16:51:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 409/652] feature:Add eic770x OTP driver

Changelogs:
In some cases, it may be necessary to read OTP information from user
space in Linux. Therefore, an OTP driver has been added, which mainly
includes two functions:

1.Reading a specific OTP field. Usage:
First, run:
     echo <field name> > /sys/kernel/debug/eswin_otp/read_field
Then, read the value:
     cat /sys/kernel/debug/eswin_otp/read_field

2.Reading a specific OTP bit. Usage:
First, run:
    echo <bit offset> > /sys/kernel/debug/eswin_otp/read_bit
Then, read the value:
    cat /sys/kernel/debug/eswin_otp/read_bit

Signed-off-by: huangyifeng <huangyifeng@eswincomputing.com>
